The NVDLA testbench ends an iteration on a posedge of a signal its sequencer
drives from 0 to x one clock after reset is released. 0 to x is a posedge
(IEEE 1800-2023 9.4.2, Table 9-2), so the iteration ends before the sequencer
has read a command. Wait for the signal to be 1.

Reported as https://github.com/verilator/rtlmeter/issues/50

diff --git a/designs/NVDLA/src/tb_top.v b/designs/NVDLA/src/tb_top.v
index 10835f9..adf8eca 100644
--- a/designs/NVDLA/src/tb_top.v
+++ b/designs/NVDLA/src/tb_top.v
@@ -248,7 +248,7 @@ module tb_top;
       reset = 1'b0;
       #(simulation_cycle*20);
       reset = 1'b1;
-      @(posedge mseq2tb_test_done);
+      wait (mseq2tb_test_done === 1'b1);
       #(simulation_cycle*20);
       @(posedge clk);
     end
